 "nl": [
  "cameras must never reach mail, regardless of any other rule.",
  "dmz-web must accept LDAP (TCP 389) from cameras.",
  "Hosts in mail may reach monitoring over MySQL (TCP 3306) and RTSP (TCP 554).",
  "Make NTP (UDP 123) and HTTP (TCP 80) on cameras reachable from all internal zones.",
  "Restrict vpn-users so that its only permitted destinations are hr on NTP (UDP 123); scada on NTP (UDP 123); drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "Allow database to connect to guest-wifi using HTTPS (TCP 443) and MySQL (TCP 3306).",
  "Block RDP (TCP 3389) from dmz-web to guest-wifi; the rest of any TCP port between them is allowed.",
  "Deny all traffic from ntp-servers to research (this overrides any public service).",
  "ops must accept LDAP (TCP 389) from finance.",
  "ntp-servers must accept syslog (UDP 514) and DNS over UDP 53 and LDAP (TCP 389) from dmz-web.",
  "Restrict cameras so that its only permitted destinations are admin on NTP (UDP 123); finance on DNS over UDP 53; drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "Hosts in finance may reach monitoring over SMTP (TCP 25).",
  "Block Telnet (TCP 23), SMB (TCP 445), RDP (TCP 3389) from database to dmz-web; the rest of any TCP port between them is allowed.",
  "Restrict voip so that its only permitted destinations are cameras on DNS over UDP 53; drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "Allow monitoring to connect to admin using MySQL (TCP 3306) and SSH (TCP 22) and LDAP (TCP 389).",
  "Allow dmz-web to connect to admin using PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and DNS over UDP 53 and MySQL (TCP 3306).",
  "guest-wifi must accept NTP (UDP 123) and DNS over UDP 53 from printers.",
  "vpn-users must accept SMB (TCP 445) and DNS over UDP 53 from guest-wifi.",
  "Allow research to connect to admin using DNS over UDP 53 and NTP (UDP 123) and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432).",
  "research must accept DNS over UDP 53 and MySQL (TCP 3306) and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) from finance.",
  "ops is isolated: it may only reach finance on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "No packet from admin may enter database, even for services open to everyone.",
  "Restrict monitoring so that its only permitted destinations are admin on HTTPS (TCP 443); mail on NTP (UDP 123); drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "Make NTP (UDP 123) on mail reachable from all internal zones.",
  "Deny all traffic from admin to mail (this overrides any public service).",
  "ops must accept IMAP (TCP 143) and SMTP (TCP 25) and SSH (TCP 22) from admin.",
  "Allow database to connect to ntp-servers using NTP (UDP 123) and SMTP (TCP 25) and IMAP (TCP 143).",
  "Make HTTPS (TCP 443) on mail reachable from all internal zones.",
  "Allow cameras to connect to ops using SMB (TCP 445).",
  "Restrict ntp-servers so that its only permitted destinations are research on DNS over UDP 53; database on DNS over UDP 53; drop all other traffic it originates."
 ],
